{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Go, you (lekh lekha)</b> — begins with a utterance in the language by which the world was created, for by ten utterances the world was created, and all of it was created only for the merit of Abraham; therefore the word מאמר is written of him." "<b>Go, you (lekh lekha)</b> — hinted to him: when you are one hundred years old, as the numerical value of לך לך, then 'I will make you a great nation' — for Isaac was born to him. Another interpretation: hinted to him that after you go from your land you will live, as the numerical value of לך לך, for he was seventy-five years old when he departed and all his years were one hundred seventy-five. Another interpretation: hinted to him the two exiles, for two times Israel will go into exile. Another interpretation: hinted to him that after fifty generations, as the numerical value of לך, they will go into exile in the days of Zedekiah, and by your merit — that I spoke with you at the age of seventy-five years in the covenant between the pieces — they will return after seventy. Therefore juxtaposed חרן to לך לך, for in the anger (חרון אף) of HaShem they were exiled, as it says ויהי בחרן."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {1 "The manuscript note צ\"ל ע' indicates the scribe recognized that בן ע\"ה (75) should read בן ע' (70), reflecting Abraham's age at the covenant between the pieces per Genesis 15 (Abraham was 70 at the covenant, 75 at his departure from Haran, and lived to 175). The translator preserves both the erroneous reading and the correction exactly as written."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:03.495522280Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}